  "details": "Hello VRChat Team,\n\nI'd like to suggest an enhancement for the VRChat SDK regarding local space constraints. Currently, Unity does not offer default constraints in local space, which can limit the creative potential, especially for avatars and interactive objects. Implementing a system for local space constraints directly within the VRChat SDK would be incredibly beneficial. For example, it would allow developers to create avatars with multiple arms or legs, or objects that maintain fun, local interactions without global interference. This feature would greatly enhance the creative possibilities within VRChat, offering users more dynamic and engaging experiences.\n\nThank you for considering this suggestion and for your continuous efforts to improve the VRChat platform.",
